text:
The sun descending in the west, The evening star does shine;
The birds are silent in their nest, And I must seek for mine.
The moon, like a flower, In heaven’s high bower, With silent delight, Sits and smiles on the night.
Farewell, green fields and happy groves, Where flocks have took delight.
Where lambs have nibbled, silent moves The feet of angels bright;
Unseen, they pour blessing, And joy without ceasing, On each bud and blossom, And each sleeping bosom.

